# The public address this deployment is served from, with no trailing slash.
#
# It is substituted into index.html, robots.txt and sitemap.xml after the build, by
# scripts/seo-urls.mjs, for the canonical link and the share cards. A build input rather
# than a committed constant so the hostname is not baked into a public repository, and so
# a second deployment does not advertise the first one's canonical URL.
#
# Three places it can come from, in this order:
#   1. the environment — what CI and scripts/deploy.sh use
#   2. this file (dashboard/.env)
#   3. the repo root .env, which is where the VM keeps its configuration
#
# It used to be `VITE_SITE_URL`. The `VITE_` prefix means "expose this to browser code
# through import.meta.env", which nothing here does — the substitution happens in a plain
# Node script after `vite build` has finished.
#
# **Left commented out on purpose, and that changed with this file's meaning.** While
# `dashboard/.env` was silently ignored, a copied placeholder was inert. Now that the file
# is genuinely read, `cp .env.example .env` with a live value would publish a canonical
# link and a sitemap pointing at example.org — which is the exact failure seo-urls.mjs
# strips the tags to avoid. No value beats a confidently wrong one: uncomment this and put
# your own hostname in, or leave it and the tags are omitted.
#
# SITE_URL=https://your-host.example.org
